        "superseded_justification": "Judge accepted the contested divergence: mimic-fhir/sql/fhir_observation_chartevents.sql:9 casts source charttime through TIMESTAMPTZ and line 67 writes the transformed value to Observation.effectiveDateTime. Thus MIN(transform(charttime)) differs from transform(MIN(charttime)) across spring-forward gaps, accounting for seven intime_hr aggregate conflicts; the one outtime_hr conflict is directly replay-attributed to the same cast. All 8/73,181 conflicts (0.011%) are accounted for, and the original 02:mm wall times are unrecoverable from FHIR because effectiveDateTime carries only the normalized value and issued carries storetime. Resource ids are opaque and cannot recover them. The loss changes no row inclusion, stay_id key, grouping, or temporal carry-forward, and is accepted under the contract's proven-DST upstream-defect exemption.",
